{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you forget a sheaf.</b> And not a stack — from here they said: a sheaf that contains two se'ah and he forgot it — it is not שִׁכְחָה (Pe'ah 6:4)." "<b>In the field.</b> To include forgotten standing grain — that he forgot part of it from harvesting." "<b>You shall not turn back to take it.</b> From here they said: what is behind him is שִׁכְחָה; what is before him is not שִׁכְחָה, for it is not subject to בַּל תָּשׁוּב (Pe'ah 4; Bava Metzia 11)." "<b>So that He may bless you.</b> And even though it came about without his intention — קַ\"וָ for one who does it with intention. Say from this: a shekel fell from his hand and a poor man found it and was sustained by it — he is blessed on its account (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:16.599034092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}